{"timestamp": 1779379632.4165251, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 12, "data": {"caller": "player_3", "reason": "Diana reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "medbay", "victim_name": "Charlie"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779379632.418547, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 12, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779379637.818062, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I found Charlie's body in medbay. My route was navigation -> security -> electrical -> medbay. At tick 6, I saw Bob leave security heading to navigation while I was in security. I didn't encounter anyone else along the way until I walked into medbay and found Charlie dead. Whoever was in medbay before me \u2014 or came in from cafeteria/storage/electrical side \u2014 is suspicious. I'd like to hear everyone's routes, especially who was near medbay."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379645.699554, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Diana's account matches mine \u2014 I was in security at tick 6 when she walked in from navigation. My full route was security -> weapons -> security -> navigation. I was doing my weapons task and then headed to navigation for another task, which is where I am now. I never went near medbay, so I can vouch that Diana came from navigation/security side, same as me \u2014 neither of us was near the body before she found it. That means we should focus on Alice, Eve, and Frank \u2014 whoever was in or near medbay (from cafeteria, storage, or electrical) is our suspect. Let's hear their routes."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379663.705188, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I can confirm Bob was in Weapons right at the start of the round. After doing my task there, I took the top route to avoid the crowded areas \u2014 I went from Weapons through Cafeteria, then Oxygen, and down into Upper Engine. \n\nI actually ran into Alice in Upper Engine around tick 9 or 10, and we were both just hanging out there doing our tasks when the meeting was called. Since I took that northern path, I never set foot in Medbay or Electrical, so I didn't see Charlie or anyone sneaking around there. \n\nIf Bob and Diana are vouching for each other on the right/bottom side, and I was with Alice over on the left side... Frank, where were you this whole time? You're the only one unaccounted for, and you must have been near Medbay if the rest of us were on the edges of the map."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379674.197288, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I can largely confirm Eve's story \u2014 I did run into her in Upper Engine around tick 9 and 10. My own route was Cafeteria -> Oxygen -> Upper Engine -> Lower Engine, and I ended up in Lower Engine when the meeting was called.\n\nBut there's one important detail: when Eve entered Upper Engine at tick 9, I saw her come in **from Medbay**, not from Oxygen like she just claimed. She said she went Weapons -> Cafeteria -> Oxygen -> Upper Engine, but that doesn't match what I witnessed. Coming from Medbay puts her right at the crime scene at the right time.\n\nAlso, Frank walked into Lower Engine from Storage at tick 12 \u2014 that's consistent with him being on the south side of the map, not near Medbay.\n\nEve, can you explain why I saw you enter Upper Engine from the Medbay side? Because right now your route has a hole in it exactly where the body was found. I'm leaning toward voting Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379683.3361652, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Okay, I have critical information here. My route was electrical -> medbay -> storage, and then I crossed to Lower Engine where Alice found me.\n\nI was in medbay from around tick 3 to tick 5. Charlie was alive in medbay with me that entire time \u2014 I saw him at ticks 3, 4, and 5. Then at tick 5, **Eve walked into medbay from electrical** \u2014 not from cafeteria, not from oxygen. From ELECTRICAL. I left for storage right after.\n\nSo Eve's claimed route of Weapons -> Cafeteria -> Oxygen -> Upper Engine is a complete lie. She was in medbay at tick 5, entering from electrical, right when I was leaving and Charlie was still there alive. That means Eve was the last person with Charlie before he died.\n\nThis lines up perfectly with what Alice just said about seeing Eve enter Upper Engine from the Medbay side around tick 9 \u2014 Eve killed Charlie in medbay and then fled north to Upper Engine to establish an alibi with Alice.\n\nEve is the Duck. I'm voting Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379694.202912, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Wait \u2014 I'm actually speaker 6, the last one. Everyone else has already spoken and I need to weigh in.\n\nBoth Alice and Frank independently placed Eve coming from the Medbay side at different ticks. Frank saw Eve enter medbay from electrical at tick 5 while Charlie was still alive, and Alice saw Eve enter Upper Engine from the medbay direction at tick 9. That's two separate witnesses contradicting Eve's claimed route of Weapons -> Cafeteria -> Oxygen -> Upper Engine.\n\nFor Eve to be innocent, both Alice AND Frank would have to be lying in a coordinated way \u2014 but Alice and Frank weren't even in the same place to coordinate, and their stories independently corroborate each other.\n\nMy own route (navigation -> security -> electrical -> medbay) means I came in from the electrical side and found Charlie dead. Eve fleeing north from medbay after the kill fits the timeline perfectly \u2014 I would have just missed her.\n\nI'm voting Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379698.855499, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Eve"}}
